     [38;5;246mIn-app instant; email batched per user every ~15 min, with an opt-in daily digest. One email per burst of activity
[39m     [38;5;246minstead of one per edit. Near-free given the worker already exists.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Immediate per change
     [38;5;246mEvery notifiable change sends its own email right away. Lowest latency and simplest to implement and debug, but [39m
     [38;5;246mnoisy — a lively task can produce a burst of near-identical mail.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Daily digest only
     [38;5;246mOne email per person per day summarizing everything. Quietest possible inbox and trivially predictable, but useless
[39m     [38;5;246mfor anything time-sensitive; urgent changes wait until tomorrow.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Per-user choice, no default opinion
     [38;5;246mShip all three modes and let each person pick. Most flexible, but it's three code paths to build and test, and [39m
     [38;5;246msomeone still has to choose what new users get.[39m
